### Step 6: Initial Execution & Granting OAuth Consent
To allow the script to read directory metadata and usage reports, Google requires an explicit, one-time administrator authorization.

1. At the top of the Apps Script editor, locate the **Run / Debug** toolbar.
2. Verify that the function dropdown displays:
   `generateDomainUsageReport`
3. Click the **Run** button (▶️).
4. An **Authorization required** popup window will appear. Click **Review permissions**.
5. Select your Google Workspace Administrator account.
6. **Google Security Warning Screen:**
   Because this script is created directly within your organization's tenant and has not been submitted for public Marketplace review, Google displays:
   `Google hasn’t verified this app`.
   * Click the small text link that says **Advanced** in the lower-left corner of the dialog.
   * Click **Go to Workspace Telemetry Suite (unsafe)** at the bottom. *(Note: This warning is standard for custom internal tenant automations).*
7. The permissions consent screen will display the exact scopes requested:
   * Connect to an external service (`UrlFetchApp`).
   * View customer usage reports for your domain.
   * View customers and user info on your domain.
   * View and manage license assignments.
   * See, edit, create, and delete your spreadsheets.
8. Click **Allow**.
9. The script will execute. You will see an **Execution log** stream in the bottom panel. Within 15–30 seconds, an administrative alert will indicate successful completion.

### Step 7: Running via the Custom Spreadsheet Menu
Once authorized, you never need to open the Apps Script editor again.

1. Return to your Google Sheet browser tab and refresh the page (`F5` or `Ctrl + R`).
2. In the top spreadsheet menu (next to *Help*), a new native menu will appear:
   **Workspace Governance**
3. Click **Workspace Governance** > **Generate Complete Usage & Subscription Report**.
4. The script will run in the background, pull the latest reconciled telemetry, and refresh all three tabs automatically.
